# Accepted risk, reviewed 2026-11-14. Re-check when upgrading cryptography.
# python-cryptography < 49/50: PKCS#7 parsing issues. DocScan never parses PKCS#7 data;
# cryptography is only a transitive dependency of PyMySQL (MySQL caching_sha2_password handshake).
# Fixed versions (>=49/50) currently crash with SIGILL on arm64 Linux VMs (Colima/Apple Silicon),
# which breaks local development, so we stay on the 46.x line until that is resolved upstream.
CVE-2026-69247
CVE-2026-69249
# Bundled OpenSSL in cryptography wheels (fixed in 48.0.1, same SIGILL problem as above).
# Exposure: the library is only used client-side for the MySQL auth handshake, on a private network.
